.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
All of these functions were removed since OpenSSL 4.0.  If there is still a need
for these definitions to present (despite the support for engines being absent),
it is possible to define the \fBOPENSSL_ENGINE_STUB\fR macro (before the inclusion
of the \f(CW\*(C`openssl/engine.h\*(C'\fR header) to get stub definitions of the
aforementioned functions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
.IP \fBOPENSSL_ENGINES\fR 4
.IX Item "OPENSSL_ENGINES"
This environment variable was removed in OpenSSL 4.0.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.IX Header "RETURN VALUES"
When the \fBOPENSSL_ENGINE_STUB\fR macro is defined, these functions will always
fail and will return either NULL or 0 depending on the nature of the function.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBopenssl_user_macros\fR\|(7)
.SH HISTORY
.IX Header "HISTORY"
All of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
.PP
\&\fBENGINE_cleanup()\fR was deprecated in OpenSSL 1.1.0 by the automatic cleanup
done by \fBOPENSSL_cleanup()\fR and should not be used.
.PP
All of these functions were removed in OpenSSL 4.0.
